  "answer": "Based on my research, here are the U.S. Presidents who meet all three criteria:\n\n**1. Theodore Roosevelt**\n- Attended: **Harvard University** (AAU founding member, 1900)\n- Governor: New York (1899–1900)\n- Elected president: 1904 (succeeded McKinley in 1901, then won election in 1904)\n\n**2. Woodrow Wilson**\n- Attended: **Princeton University** (AAU founding member, 1900)\n- Governor: New Jersey (1911–1913)\n- Elected president: 1912\n\n**3. Franklin D. Roosevelt**\n- Attended: **Harvard University** (AAU founding member, 1900)\n- Governor: New York (1929–1932)\n- Elected president: 1932\n\n**4. Jimmy Carter**\n- Attended: **Georgia Institute of Technology** (AAU member since 2010)\n- Governor: Georgia (1971–1975)\n- Elected president: 1976\n\n**5. George W. Bush**\n- Attended: **Yale University** (AAU founding member, 1900)\n- Governor: Texas (1995–2000)\n- Elected president: 2000\n\n---\n\n**Excluded for failing one or more criteria:**\n- **Calvin Coolidge** — Amherst College (not an AAU member)\n- **Ronald Reagan** — Eureka College (not an AAU member)\n- **Bill Clinton** — Georgetown University (not an AAU member)\n- **Rutherford B. Hayes, Grover Cleveland, William McKinley** — Elected before 1900",
